{
  "id": "EUVD-2026-124675",
  "enisaUuid": "38a4a6c9-4770-3887-a2a6-1a03c507144b",
  "description": "A flaw was found in Foreman\u2019s Api::V2::PersonalAccessTokensController, where Foreman::Controller::UserAware#find_user resolves the target account using User.find(params[:user_id]) without applying the required parent-user authorization check. An attacker with the create_personal_access_tokens permission can therefore invoke POST /api/v2/users/:user_id/personal_access_tokens with another user\u2019s ID and create a Personal Access Token on their behalf. The resulting plaintext token is returned in the API response, while PersonalAccessToken#check_permissions_after_save only validates create_personal_access_tokens on the token and does not enforce edit_users authorization on the target user. The attacker can then use the forged token to authenticate as the victim, potentially resulting in complete account takeover, including administrator accounts.",
  "datePublished": "Nov 12, 2026, 8:19:29 PM",
